# Line endings.
#
# Developed on macOS, built in Linux containers, so LF everywhere: a Windows
# checkout cannot then feed CRLF into the Docker build. 28 scaffolded Identity
# pages were CRLF when this file was added - the ASP.NET Identity scaffolder
# writes CRLF - which is exactly the drift this prevents recurring.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are LF or they do not run in a container at all.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Recorded wire data. Left byte-exact: these are evidence of what a printer
# actually sent, and tests replay them. Normalising a record would defeat the
# point of keeping one.
*.capture -text
*.cap -text

# Vendored client assets, restored by LibMan from libman.json. Third-party
# bytes we do not own, so they are left exactly as shipped rather than
# normalised. (Note: .gitignore lists this directory, but some files under it
# were committed before that entry existed and are still tracked.)
Homespool.Host/wwwroot/lib/** -text

# Binary.
*.ico binary

# Not a guard against source-file encoding. `working-tree-encoding=UTF-8` was
# tried and is a no-op: when the declared encoding is already UTF-8 git skips
# the conversion, so it never validates - a Latin-1 .cs file is staged without
# complaint. Silent U+FFFD corruption on every SDK tested (6.0/8.0/10.0) is the
# real hazard; catching it needs a check that reads the files, not an attribute.
